<p>I really like this - the understated, clinical tone works very well, and the mystery is maintained nicely.</p>
<p>A nitpick: in &quot;Specifically, regions of SCP-2838-1's head corresponding &#8230;&quot; you're refering to SCP-2838-1 as a single entity, whereas in the rest of the piece you use &quot;SCP-2838-1 instances&quot;.</p>
<p>In my headcannon, it's not certain that they're burning. Thermoreception areas are also highly stimulated from intense cold, and the surrounding environment is much colder than their surface temperatures. They might be freezing forever. Or the foundation might have mismapped their brains.</p>
<p>Definite +1.</p>

